<section class="hero">
  <h1>What Daily Conviction <em>Bought</em></h1>
  <div class="hero-subtitle">What did a small bitcoin buy, made every single day, actually add up to?</div>
  <p class="subtitle">Pick a start date and a daily amount. The page replays that habit against bitcoin's real price history &mdash; what it accumulated, what it cost, what it's worth now, and what the ride felt like along the way.</p>
</section>

<main class="content-area">
  {% include 'components/tool-framing.njk' %}

  <section class="section-intro">
    <p class="dc-lead-prose">The story that gets passed around is a specific one: $30 of bitcoin, bought every single day since January 2017. Rather than retell it, this page recomputes it live &mdash; and lets you change the numbers. The famous run is the starting point &mdash; its million-dollar crossing was covered by <a href="https://www.benzinga.com/markets/cryptocurrency/24/11/42170334/bitcoin-investor-turns-daily-30-purchases-into-1-million-portfolio-in-7-years-10-months-an" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Benzinga</a> and <a href="https://crypto.news/30-to-1m-how-this-bitcoin-investor-turned-spare-change-into-seven-figures/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">crypto.news</a>, and retold in <a href="https://lastcoinstanding.substack.com/p/the-bitcoin-exit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the essay this tool grew out of</a>. Every other start date and amount is one drag away. It is the record of what a habit did, not a recommendation to run one.</p>
  </section>

